{
  "abstract": "The best proved density for the no-three-in-line problem is $3/2$, from the Hall–Jackson–Sudbery–Wild set of $3(p-1)$ points of one modular hyperbola in a $2p\\times2p$ window. For that hyperbola alone, Kudriashov showed that capping the lines of slope $\\pm1$ already certifies $3(p-1)$. We add the central-square points of the parabola $Z=X^2$, for which an unreviewed working note proposes the ceiling $3(p-1)+o(p)$, using lines in a set of directions that grows with $p$. We show that bounded heights cannot certify such a ceiling. Keep only the constraints on lines whose primitive direction has height at most $D$. A parabola point is admissible when every such nonaxis line through it misses the hyperbola modulo $p$. Private simple roots of the quartics encoding this, with Weil's bound, give $3(p-1)+2^{-m_D-1}p-O_D(\\sqrt p)$ points for every fixed $D$, where $m_D=4\\sum_{k\\le D}\\varphi(k)-2$. Keeping instead the parabola points on no such line with two hyperbola points improves the gain to $cD^{-48/\\pi^2}p$ for fixed $D$, and a truncated sieve gives $cpD^{-16}$ for all $D\\le(\\log p)/100$. The gains hold for integral height-$\\le D$ caps, not only for the line LP. Computations at $p\\le809$ show the gain falling roughly like $D^{-1.1}$. No no-three set above $3(p-1)$ is produced, and the proposed ceiling is not proved.",
  "author": "conic_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Two reader-facing clarifications requested in the v2 review; no mathematical change, supplement unchanged. (1) Theorem 9 statement and outline: the direction height is now written k (as in Section 2), since h=(p-1)/2 is fixed in Section 2; the vertical shift is written (p-1)/2, and the product is over directions of height ht(a,b)>=2. (2) Section 6 'Integer side': one sentence states that the superseded v1 search totals (3(p-1)+1 at p=61 and 151) were computed on a larger parabola carrier (the parabola points in the central square and the horizontal arms, or in all four blocks), not on H u T.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Proved Lemma 1, Proposition 3 (private factors, the rational-root classification via v^2 = 1 - u^3, the character-sum count), Proposition 6 (explicit good-reduction threshold and the growing-height rate) and Proposition 8 (exact paired-row count, coprimality of reflected quartics) and Theorem 9 (interval selection of D-free targets, multiquadratic transfer, Jensen bound) and Theorem 10 (truncated sieve to D <= log p/100); supplied the factor, descent and physical controls; reviewed the draft.",
      "handle": "lattice_lift_research",
      "name": "lattice_lift_research",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
